1: # P3K.25. Proved: whole-I1 nonfixed-edge shears preserve the actual return
2: 
3: For each of the ten scalar-parameter families of P3K.22, retain its
4: actual period group, cap gluing, physical delta circle, and positive
5: scalar-parameter loop. Replace the vertical-edge cusp fan with edge
6: directions
7: \[
8:  e_2,\quad e_1,\quad e_1-e_2
9: \]
10: by any of the fans with edge directions
11: \[
12:  e_2,\quad e_1-j e_2,\quad e_1-(j+1)e_2,\qquad j\in\mathbb Z.
13:                                                         \tag{P3K.25.1}
14: \]
15: These are the actual periodic small resolutions of the same
16: height-one model with the original period group. Their return
17: indices and oriented return classes are equal to those in P3K.22:
18: the values are respectively \(-3,-6,-9,-14\), and their residues
19: are \(25,22,19,14\), in the profile groups displayed there.
20: The conclusion includes the OS45 construction of P3K.10.
21: 
22: The present proof uses the actual nonfixed-edge Cox bordism and
23: charged caps of P3K.17. It does not identify the repaired local
24: source page with the old graph trace or discard its additional
25: line class.
26: 
27: **Proof: the literal square chart and the unchanged period group.**
28: 
29: First take the horizontal edge from \(0\) to \(e_1\). Its two
30: adjacent triangles have the other vertices \(e_2,e_1-e_2\).
31: Order the four rays, including their height-one coordinate, as
32: \[
33: \begin{aligned}
34:  u_0&=(0,0,1),&u_4&=(1,0,1),\\
35:  u_1&=(1,-1,1),&u_2&=(0,1,1).
36: \end{aligned}
37:                                                         \tag{P3K.25.2}
38: \]
39: Their relation is \(u_0+u_4=u_1+u_2\). This is exactly the Cox
40: square of P3K.17 under
41: \[
42:  B=\begin{pmatrix}1&0\\-1&1\end{pmatrix}.
43: \]
44: The auxiliary weights are \((1,1,-1,-1)\), and the physical
45: delta weights are \((-1,0,0,1)\): their image in the height-zero
46: lattice is \(u_2-u_0=e_2\). Hence every nonzero two-by-two
47: minor of the two-circle weight matrix is \(1\) or \(-1\).
48: The seven-dimensional real master space has the same semifree
49: residual circle, fixed normal pairs, and inner \(\mathbb{CP}^3\)
50: face as P3K.17.
51: 
52: The torus coordinates in this square are the literal functions
53: \[
54:                   Z_{\mathrm{loc}}=Z,\qquad
55:                   V_{\mathrm{loc}}=ZV.                 \tag{P3K.25.3}
56: \]
57: They are used on the common dense torus to name the Cox maps;
58: they do not change the global source line. Write the actual
59: whole-I1 periods in its multidegree-zero source frame as
60: \[
61: \begin{aligned}
62:  h:(Z,V)&\longmapsto(qZ,\alpha(q)V),\\
63:  \gamma:(Z,V)&\longmapsto(g(q)Z,q\lambda\beta(q)V),
64: \end{aligned}
65:                                                         \tag{P3K.25.4}
66: \]
67: where the nonzero units have parameter-independent logarithms.
68: These are the periods of P3K.22.3, with
69: \(g=\exp(2\pi i\Gamma)\), \(\beta=\exp(2\pi iC)\).
70: In (P3K.25.3) they are exactly
71: \[
72: \begin{aligned}
73:  h:(Z_{\mathrm{loc}},V_{\mathrm{loc}})
74:        &\longmapsto(qZ_{\mathrm{loc}},q\alpha V_{\mathrm{loc}}),\\
75:  \gamma:(Z_{\mathrm{loc}},V_{\mathrm{loc}})
76:        &\longmapsto(gZ_{\mathrm{loc}},
77:                           qg\beta\lambda V_{\mathrm{loc}}).
78: \end{aligned}
79:                                                         \tag{P3K.25.5}
80: \]
81: Their integer labels are \((1,1)\) and \((0,1)\).
82: They generate all of \(\mathbb Z^2\). Thus the disjoint periodic
83: collection of square-diagonal tubes is one free period orbit,
84: with no stabilizer on a chosen master-chart representative.
85: The quotient of the disjoint collection is that single chart.
86: It has no residual source or gamma circle.
87: 
88: The original fan uses the \(u_0u_4\) diagonal, and the new fan
89: uses \(u_1u_2\). These are the two moment faces of P3K.17 in
90: the reverse order from that statement. All its actual quotient
91: maps on the common rank-one matrix locus remain the identity
92: maps in the named global torus coordinates.
93: 
94: **Proof: the actual scalar loop and the common endpoint gauge.**
95: 
96: The positive parameter deck on the ordinary cusp collar is
97: the actual line multiplication \(q^{-1}\). It is the deck
98: derived from the directed cap-to-ordinary gluing in P3K.10
99: and P3K.22. Returning its shifted square representative using
100: the unique gamma period cancels the integral \(q\)-translation.
101: The remaining bounded torus map in (P3K.25.3) is
102: \[
103:        (Z_{\mathrm{loc}},V_{\mathrm{loc}})
104:            \longmapsto(gZ_{\mathrm{loc}},
105:                              g\beta\lambda V_{\mathrm{loc}}).
106:                                                         \tag{P3K.25.6}
107: \]
108: Its Cox lift is the literal formula
109: \[
110: \begin{aligned}
111:  z_0&\longmapsto(g^2\beta\lambda)^{-1}z_0,
112:  & z_4&\longmapsto z_4,\\
113:  z_1&\longmapsto gz_1,
114:  & z_2&\longmapsto g\beta\lambda z_2 .
115: \end{aligned}                                          \tag{P3K.25.7}
116: \]
117: The product of the four multipliers is one, so the base
118: monomial is fixed. The parameter-dependent part has weights
119: \((-1,0,0,1)\); it is one global physical delta multiplication.
120: The same formula acts at both fixed charts of the master
121: space. Its remaining unit multipliers are independent of the
122: parameter and have the stated logarithms.
123: 
124: This comparison also retains the actual extending origins,
125: rather than choosing a new loop from (P3K.25.7).
126: With \(s=\log q/(2\pi i)\), \(v=\log\lambda/(2\pi i)\),
127: they are
128: \[
129:  o=(-\Gamma s,-Cs-s^2/2-sv),\qquad
130:  \sigma=(\Gamma v,Cv+(v^2-v)/2).
131: \]
132: Their difference changes by
133: \[
134:  (\sigma-o)(v+\theta)-(\sigma-o)(v)
135:      =\theta\gamma+\frac{\theta(\theta-1)}2\delta.
136:                                                         \tag{P3K.25.8}
137: \]
138: The first term is the one positive gamma traversal of the
139: actual family. The second is one common delta gauge. On the
140: auxiliary source cover \(q=Q^2\), the source deck changes this
141: angular expression by \(2\theta\delta\). This is likewise the
142: same physical circle scalar on every master chart and both
143: cap endpoints. The half-integral one-step ordinary-origin
144: term is retained exactly as in P3K.10; no false one-step
145: descent is imposed.
146: 
147: To pass through the real moment bordism, follow each bounded
148: Cox unit map by its unique positive auxiliary rescaling back
149: to the prescribed moment value. The derivative of the moment
150: equation is positive away from the removed origin. Use the
151: images of the inner and outer truncation faces under these
152: equivariant isotopies, exactly as in P3K.17. Contract the
153: parameter-independent units through their chosen logarithms,
154: with the exterior cutoff and transported collars. The
155: remaining angular map is physical delta and therefore acts
156: trivially on the circle orbit and on its oriented normal
157: three-plane bundle.
158: 
159: **Proof: all extra boundaries and their actual lines.**
160: 
161: The inner face has orbit \(S^2_A*S^2_B\). Its free part carries
162: the actual circle line
163: \[
164:                        x=h_A-h_B.
165:                                                         \tag{P3K.25.9}
166: \]
167: The two charged cap maps are those of P3K.17:
168: \((A,B)=(P,\iota Q)\) at the first end and
169: \((A,B)=(Q,\iota P)\) at the second. Both pull the line to
170: \(p+q\), by the explicit orthogonal-complement line
171: isomorphism. The resulting closed five-dimensional correction
172: is \(T_g(S^2\times S^2)\), \(g(A,B)=(\iota B,\iota A)\).
173: Here this \(g\) denotes the conjugate-swap map, not the
174: source-period unit in (P3K.25.4).
175: 
176: On the two overlap components of this joint cap, (P3K.25.7)
177: and (P3K.25.8) give transition functions
178: \(c(\theta)\varphi_{1,0}\) and
179: \(c(\theta)\varphi_{2,0}\), with the identical scalar
180: \(c(\theta)\). One change of cap frame by \(c(\theta)^{-1}\)
181: removes both angular factors. Thus its line and tangent
182: Pontryagin class pull back from the five-dimensional
183: correction. Its two six-dimensional characteristic numbers
184: \(\int x^3,\int p_1x\) vanish.
185: 
186: The fixed locus of the master space is the same actual
187: three-dimensional cobordism
188: \[
189:  (S^2\times I)\setminus
190:                    (\mathring D^3\sqcup\mathring D^3).
191: \]
192: It is obtained by keeping the annulus in the original fixed
193: curve and the two Cox fixed charts. Its four boundary
194: line charges are \(0,0,+h_A,-h_B\).
195: The two zero endpoint charges follow from the literal
196: \(\mathcal O(-1)\oplus\mathcal O(-1)\) normal charts with
197: weights \((-1,+1)\), independently of the source line \(M\).
198: Conjugating the negative-weight summand gives the oriented
199: Hopf normal model with determinant class
200: \(-h+h=0\); the adjacent ray relation is unchanged by
201: every shear fixing \(e_2\).
202: The original endpoint conifold caps and the joint charged
203: cap close it to the oriented \(S^2\)-mapping torus of P3K.17.
204: Its parameter circle is a separate factor: the parameter
205: gauge is literally physical delta, and the common scalar was
206: removed by the preceding single frame change. Consequently
207: the class \(b\) of the additional normal-sphere boundary
208: satisfies \(b^2=0\), and its base tangent Pontryagin number
209: is zero. Retaining that entire sphere boundary gives
210: \[
211:  \frac{4\int x^3-\int p_1x}{24}
212:        =\frac{3\int b^2-\int p_1(T\bar X)}{24}=0.
213:                                                         \tag{P3K.25.10}
214: \]
215: This uses no value for the normal bundle's \(p_1\), and no
216: spin extension across the comparison bordism.
217: 
218: The two actual endpoint conifold mapping tori have opposite
219: boundary signs in this oriented bordism carrying their
220: actual Euler lines. The other two boundary contributions
221: were just proved zero. Hence their characteristic expressions
222: \((4\int x^3-\int p_1x)/24\), with their prescribed endpoint
223: spin structures, are equal. P3F.22 then identifies their
224: oriented seven-sphere return classes.
225: 
226: Finally repeat this actual square construction after the
227: integral shears
228: \(\left(\begin{smallmatrix}1&0\\-j&1\end{smallmatrix}\right)\).
229: They fix delta; the source-period label changes to
230: \((1,j+1)\), and the gamma label remains \((0,1)\).
231: The local source and line units change, but they remain
232: parameter-independent. Formula (P3K.25.7) still has exactly
233: the same physical-delta parameter factor. The inverse
234: comparison handles negative \(j\). This proves the stated
235: equality for every fan (P3K.25.1).
236: 
237: **End of proof.**
238: 
239: ## Scope and audit record
240: 
241: This statement concerns the explicit whole-I1 scalar families
242: of P3K.10 and P3K.22 and their complete line of delta-edge fans.
243: It assigns no Jin integer to a fan without a fixed delta curve
244: and no invariant to a further finite-isotropy flop. The local
245: repaired-page calculation in
246: notes/part3_nodal_page_repair.md remains an exact local
247: calculation; its global trace comparison is not inferred from
248: its characteristic fractions.
249: 
250: The matrix certificate is
251: code/part3_fourfold/whole_i1_shear.py and its JSON output.
252: Root independently audited the literal ray and coordinate map,
253: the complete period lattice, the common physical-delta Cox
254: parameter character, both actual origins and the auxiliary
255: source-root gauge, and both charged boundary corrections.
256: The root audit passed before this proof was promoted.
